            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The spot is shady, damp or holds water, and probably has cracks or debris for moss to anchor in. Treating the moss without changing those conditions only buys time. Trim overhanging branches, redirect water, sweep debris regularly, fill cracks and keep the surface sealed."
          }
        },
