          "name": "Should I seal my driveway after removing moss?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If the sealer has worn through, yes. A sealed surface sheds water and gives moss less to grip. Make sure the drive is fully dry and all treatment residue is rinsed off, fill cracks first, and choose a day with suitable temperatures and no rain for at least 24 hours."
