        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Scrape first on a dry day, treat what is left with one product used safely, and clear the dead growth with a broom or a gentle pass of a pressure washer. Then fill cracks and reseal if the surface has worn, so water runs off instead of soaking in.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The lasting fix is changing the conditions. More sun, better drainage and a clean, sealed surface turn a moss-prone driveway into one that needs little more than a seasonal sweep.
          </p>
